    {"unit": "W01-14", "code": "RA", "page": null, "position": null, "drift": false, "reasoning_stated": null, "note": "Quick identification is in the values heading (p. 630) and efficiency is a stated concern (p. 631). Table 2's narcotics values cell names only variety and autonomy, and is silent on speed (p. 633)."},
    {"unit": "W01-15", "code": "P", "page": "p. 621; p. 632; p. 633; p. 635", "position": null, "drift": false, "reasoning_stated": false, "note": "Table 2 coding (p. 633), the p. 635 statement and the firearms challenges (p. 621) are printed. Where the crystal-testing Daubert hearing took place is not printed; the analyst heard of it at a workshop (p. 632). Placing it in other jurisdictions is a judgment from her contrast with Metropolitan County and from p. 635."},
    {"unit": "W01-16", "code": "N", "page": null, "position": null, "drift": false, "reasoning_stated": null, "note": ""},
    {"unit": "W02-01", "code": "RA", "page": null, "position": null, "drift": false, "reasoning_stated": null, "note": "In the pp. 635–636 paragraph, the challenge is called potential and the toxicologists' outcome is named only as interaction and action around change. Apart from saying they saw an opportunity to change practices, the paragraph states no content."},
