    {"unit": "W03-04", "code": "C", "page": "p. 627; p. 633", "position": "warrant", "drift": false, "reasoning_stated": null, "note": "The author also links toxicology to DNA outside the attorney's argument. Toxicologists are said to have read the pressure to be like DNA narrowly (p. 627). Table 2 says DNA's error-measurement practices matched their values and technique (p. 633)."},
